  "body": [
    {
      "tag": "div",
      "attributes": {},
      "children": [
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "prathamo niḥṣyandaḥ",
          "translated_text": "The first effusion",
          "segment_number": 1
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yasyonmeṣanimeṣābhyāṃ jagataḥ pralayodayau |",
              "translated_text": "By whose opening and closing of the eyes, the dissolution and creation of the world occur,",
              "segment_number": 2
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "taṃ śakticakravibhavaprabhavaṃ śaṅkaraṃ stumaḥ || 1 ||",
              "translated_text": "we praise <s>Śaṅkara</s>, the origin of the power and glory of the <s>Śakti</s> circle.",
              "segment_number": 3
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yatra sthitam idaṃ sarvaṃ kāryaṃ yasmāc ca nirgataṃ |",
              "translated_text": "Where this entire effect is situated, from which it has emerged,",
              "segment_number": 4
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tasyānāvṛtarūpatvān na nirodho 'sti kutracit || 2 ||",
              "translated_text": "because of its unobstructed nature, there is no cessation anywhere.",
              "segment_number": 5
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "jāgradādi vibhede 'pi tadabhinne prasarpati |",
              "translated_text": "Even in the distinctions such as waking, it pervades in its undivided form,",
              "segment_number": 6
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nivartate nijānnaiva svabhāvād upalabdhṛtaḥ || 3 ||",
              "translated_text": "it does not withdraw from its own nature due to the perceiver.",
              "segment_number": 7
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ahaṃ sukhī ca duḥkhī ca raktaś ca ityadisamvidaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "\"I am happy, I am sorrowful, I am attached,\" such cognitions,",
              "segment_number": 8
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sukhādyavasthānusyūte vartante 'nyatra tāḥ sphuṭam || 4 ||",
              "translated_text": "clearly exist elsewhere, interwoven with states of happiness and the like.",
              "segment_number": 9
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "na duḥkhaṃ na sukhaṃ yatra na grāhyam grāhakaṃ na ca |",
              "translated_text": "Where there is neither sorrow nor happiness, neither the grasped nor the grasper,",
              "segment_number": 10
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "na cāsti mūḍhabhāvo 'pi tad asti paramārthataḥ || 5 ||",
              "translated_text": "nor is there a state of delusion, that exists in the highest reality.",
              "segment_number": 11
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yataḥ karaṇavargo 'yaṃ vimūḍho 'mūḍhavat svayam |",
              "translated_text": "Since this group of instruments, though deluded, behaves like the undeluded itself,",
              "segment_number": 12
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sahāntareṇa cakreṇa pravṛttisthitisaṃhṛtiḥ || 6 ||",
              "translated_text": "with the internal wheel, there is creation, maintenance, and dissolution.",
              "segment_number": 13
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "labhate tatprayatnena parīkṣyaṃ tattvam ādarāt |",
              "translated_text": "One attains that essence through effort, examining with reverence,",
              "segment_number": 14
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yataḥ svatantratā tasya sarvatreyam akṛtrimā || 7 ||",
              "translated_text": "because its independence is this, everywhere, uncontrived.",
              "segment_number": 15
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "na hīcchānodanasyāyam prerakatvena vartate |",
              "translated_text": "For this does not function as an instigator of desire and impulse,",
              "segment_number": 16
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "api tv ātmabalasparśāt puruṣas tatsamo bhavet || 8 ||",
              "translated_text": "but by the touch of self-power, a man becomes equal to that.",
              "segment_number": 17
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nijāśuddhyāsamarthasya kartavyeṣv abhilāṣiṇaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "For one desiring action, incapable due to inner impurity,",
              "segment_number": 18
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yadā kṣobhaḥ pralīyeta tadā syāt paramam padam || 9 ||",
              "translated_text": "when the agitation dissolves, then the supreme state is attained.",
              "segment_number": 19
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tadāsyākṛtrimo dharmo jñatvakartṛtvalakṣaṇah |",
              "translated_text": "Then his uncontrived nature is characterized by knowing and doing,",
              "segment_number": 20
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yatas tadepsitaṃ sarvaṃ jānāti ca karoti ca || 10 ||",
              "translated_text": "because he knows and accomplishes all that is desired.",
              "segment_number": 21
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tam adhiṣṭhātṛbhāvena svabhāvam avalokayan |",
              "translated_text": "Observing his nature with the attitude of a ruler,",
              "segment_number": 22
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "smayamāna ivāste yas tasyeyaṃ kusṛtiḥ kutaḥ || 11 ||",
              "translated_text": "he seems to smile, for where is this bad conduct for him?",
              "segment_number": 23
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nābhāvo bhāvyatām eti na ca tatrāsty amūḍhatā |",
              "translated_text": "Non-existence does not become real, nor is there non-delusion there,",
              "segment_number": 24
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yato 'bhiyogasaṃsparśāt tadāsid iti niścayah || 12 ||",
              "translated_text": "because from the touch of effort, there is certainty that it was.",
              "segment_number": 25
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "atas tatkṛtrimaṃ jñeyaṃ sauṣuptapadavat sadā |",
              "translated_text": "Therefore, that is known as artificial, always like the state of deep sleep,",
              "segment_number": 26
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "na tv evaṃ smaryamāṇatvaṃ tat tattvam pratipadyate || 13 ||",
              "translated_text": "but such memorization does not attain that reality.",
              "segment_number": 27
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "avasthāyugalaṃ cātra kāryakartṛtvaśabditam |",
              "translated_text": "The pair of states here is termed as effect and doership,",
              "segment_number": 28
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "kāryatā kṣayiṇī tatra kartṛtvam punar akṣayam || 14 ||",
              "translated_text": "effecthood is perishable there, while doership is again imperishable.",
              "segment_number": 29
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "kāryonmukhaḥ prayatno yaḥ kevalaṃ so 'tra lupyate |",
              "translated_text": "The effort inclined towards effect alone is here destroyed,",
              "segment_number": 30
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tasmin lupte vilupto 'smīty abudhaḥ pratipadyate || 15 ||",
              "translated_text": "when that is destroyed, the ignorant assumes \"I am destroyed.\"",
              "segment_number": 31
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "na tu yo 'ntarmukho bhāvah sarvajñātvaguṇāspadam |",
              "translated_text": "But the inner-directed state, which is the abode of omniscience,",
              "segment_number": 32
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tasya lopaḥ kadācit syād anyasyānupalambhanāt || 16 ||",
              "translated_text": "its loss may sometimes occur due to the non-perception of another.",
              "segment_number": 33
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tasyopalabdhiḥ satataṃ tripadāvyabhicāriṇī |",
              "translated_text": "Its realization is always unwavering in the three states,",
              "segment_number": 34
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nityaṃ syāt suprabuddhasya tadādyante parasya tu || 17 ||",
              "translated_text": "it is eternal for the well-awakened, in the beginning and end of the other.",
              "segment_number": 35
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "jñānajñeyasvarūpiṇyā śaktyā paramayā yutaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "Endowed with the supreme power of the nature of knowledge and the known,",
              "segment_number": 36
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "padadvaye vibhur bhāti tadanyatra tu cinmayaḥ || 18 ||",
              "translated_text": "in the two states, the all-pervasive shines, but elsewhere, it is consciousness itself.",
              "segment_number": 37
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "guṇādispandaniḥṣyandāḥ sāmānyaspandasaṃśrayāt |",
              "translated_text": "The effusions of qualities and others, from the support of the general vibration,",
              "segment_number": 38
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "labdhātmalābhaḥ satataṃ syur jñasyāparipanthinaḥ || 19 ||",
              "translated_text": "having gained self-attainment, are always without obstruction for the knower.",
              "segment_number": 39
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "aprabudhadhiyas tv ete svasthitisthaganodyatāḥ |",
              "translated_text": "But for the unawakened intellects, these are inclined to obstruct their own state,",
              "segment_number": 40
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "pātayanti duruttāre ghore saṃsāravartmani || 20 ||",
              "translated_text": "they cause a fall into the difficult-to-cross, terrible path of <s>saṃsāra</s>.",
              "segment_number": 41
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ataḥ satatam udyuktaḥ spandatattvaviviktaye |",
              "translated_text": "Therefore, always engaged in distinguishing the essence of vibration,",
              "segment_number": 42
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "jāgrad eva nijam bhāvam acireṇādhigacchati || 21 ||",
              "translated_text": "one quickly realizes one's own nature even while awake.",
              "segment_number": 43
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "atikruddhaḥ prahṛṣṭo vā kiṃ karomīti vā mṛśan |",
              "translated_text": "Whether extremely angry, pleased, or pondering \"What should I do?\",",
              "segment_number": 44
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "dhāvan va yat padaṃ gacchet tatra spandaḥ pratiṣṭhitaḥ || 22 ||",
              "translated_text": "or running, whatever state one reaches, there the vibration is established.",
              "segment_number": 45
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yām avasthāṃ samālambya yad ayam mama vakṣyati |",
              "translated_text": "Relying on whatever state, whatever this one will say to me,",
              "segment_number": 46
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tadavaśyaṃ kariṣye 'ham iti saṃkalpya tiṣṭhati || 23 ||",
              "translated_text": "he stands resolved, \"I will certainly do that.\"",
              "segment_number": 47
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tām aśrityordhvamārgeṇa candrasūryāv ubhāv api |",
              "translated_text": "Relying on that, by the upward path, both <s>Candra</s> and <s>Sūrya</s>,",
              "segment_number": 48
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sauṣumne 'dhvanyastamito hitvā brahmā.ṅdagocaram || 24 ||",
              "translated_text": "having abandoned the path of <s>Sauṣumna</s>, reach the realm of <s>Brahma</s>.",
              "segment_number": 49
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tadā tasmin mahāvyomni pralīnaśaśibhāskare |",
              "translated_text": "Then, in that great sky, with the moon and sun dissolved,",
              "segment_number": 50
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sauṣuptapadavan mūḍhaḥ prabuddhaḥ syād anāvṛtaḥ || 25 ||",
              "translated_text": "like the state of deep sleep, the deluded becomes awakened, unobstructed.",
              "segment_number": 51
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "dvitīyo niḥṣyandaḥ",
          "translated_text": "The second effusion",
          "segment_number": 52
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tadākramya balam mantrāḥ sarvajñābalaśālinaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "Having seized that strength, the <s>mantras</s>, endowed with the power of omniscience,",
              "segment_number": 53
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "pravartante 'dhikārāya karaṇānīva dehinām || 1 ||",
              "translated_text": "operate for authority, like the organs for embodied beings.",
              "segment_number": 54
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tatraiva sampralīyante śāntarūpā nirañjanāḥ |",
              "translated_text": "There itself, they dissolve, peaceful in form, stainless,",
              "segment_number": 55
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sahārādhakacittena tenaite śivadharmiṇaḥ || 2 ||",
              "translated_text": "along with the mind of the worshipper, these are of the nature of <s>Śiva</s>.",
              "segment_number": 56
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yasmāt sarvamayo jīvaḥ sarvabhāvasamudbhavāt |",
              "translated_text": "Since the living being is all-pervading, from the emergence of all states,",
              "segment_number": 57
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tatsaṃvedanarūpeṇa tādātmyapratipattitaḥ || 3 ||",
              "translated_text": "by the nature of that awareness, through the realization of identity.",
              "segment_number": 58
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tasmāc chabdārthacintāsu na sāvasthā na yā śivaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "Therefore, in the contemplation of sound and meaning, there is no state which is not <s>Śiva</s>",
              "segment_number": 59
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhoktaiva bhogyabhāvena sadā sarvatra saṃsthitaḥ || 4 ||",
              "translated_text": "The enjoyer, by the nature of the enjoyable, is always established everywhere",
              "segment_number": 60
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "iti vā yasya saṃvittiḥ krīḍātvenākhilaṃ jagat |",
              "translated_text": "Thus, for whom there is awareness that the entire world is a play",
              "segment_number": 61
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "sa paśyan satataṃ yukto jīvanmukto na saṃśayaḥ || 5 ||",
              "translated_text": "He, seeing constantly, is united and liberated while living, without doubt",
              "segment_number": 62
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ayam evodayas tasya dhyeyasya dhyāyicetasi |",
              "translated_text": "This indeed is the arising of that which is to be meditated upon in the mind of the meditator",
              "segment_number": 63
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tadātmatāsamāpattir icchataḥ sādhakasya yā || 6 ||",
              "translated_text": "The attainment of identity with that, for the aspirant who desires it",
              "segment_number": 64
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "iyam evāmṛtaprāptir ayam evātmano grahaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "This indeed is the attainment of immortality, this indeed is the grasping of the self",
              "segment_number": 65
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "iyaṃ nirvāṇa-dīkṣā ca śivasadbhāvadāyini || 7 ||",
              "translated_text": "This is the initiation into liberation, which grants the true nature of <s>Śiva</s>",
              "segment_number": 66
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "tṛtīyo niḥṣyandaḥ",
          "translated_text": "The third effusion",
          "segment_number": 67
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "yathecchābhyarthito dhātā jāgrato 'rthān hṛdi sthitān",
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "somasūryodayaṃ kṛtvā sampādayati dehinaḥ || 1 |",
              "translated_text": "Having caused the rise of <s>Soma</s> and <s>Sūrya</s>, accomplishes for the embodied",
              "segment_number": 69
            }
          ],
          "translated_text": "As desired, the creator, having established the meanings in the heart while awake",
          "segment_number": 68
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tathā svapne 'py abhīṣṭārthān praṇayasyānatikramāt |",
              "translated_text": "Similarly, in dreams, the desired objects, due to the absence of transgression",
              "segment_number": 70
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "nityaṃ sphuṭataraṃ madhye sthito 'vaśyaṃ prakāśayet || 2 ||",
              "translated_text": "Always more clearly, established in the middle, will definitely reveal",
              "segment_number": 71
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "anyathā tu svatantrā syāt sṛṣṭis taddharmakatvataḥ |",
              "translated_text": "Otherwise, creation would be independent, due to its nature",
              "segment_number": 72
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "satataṃ laukikasyeva jāgratsvapnapadadvaye || 3 ||",
              "translated_text": "Always, like the worldly one, in the two states of waking and dreaming",
              "segment_number": 73
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yathā hi artho 'sphuṭo dṛṣṭaḥ sāvadhāne 'pi cetasi |",
              "translated_text": "Just as an object, indistinct, is seen even in a focused mind",
              "segment_number": 74
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhūyaḥ sphuṭataro bhāti svabalodyogabhāvitaḥ || 4 ||",
              "translated_text": "Appears clearer, enhanced by one's own effort",
              "segment_number": 75
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tathā yat paramārthena yena yatra yathā sthitam |",
              "translated_text": "Thus, that which is in reality, by which, where, as it is established",
              "segment_number": 76
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tat tathā balam ākramya na cirāt sampravartate || 5 ||",
              "translated_text": "That, thus seizing strength, does not take long to manifest",
              "segment_number": 77
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "durbalo 'pi tadākramya yataḥ kārye pravartate |",
              "translated_text": "Even the weak, seizing that, proceeds in action",
              "segment_number": 78
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ācchādayed bubhukṣāṃ ca tathā yo 'ti bubhukṣitaḥ || 6 ||",
              "translated_text": "Covers hunger, thus one who is very hungry",
              "segment_number": 79
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "anenādhiṣṭhite dehe yathā sarvajñatādayaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "In this body, established, as omniscience and others",
              "segment_number": 80
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tathā svātmany adhiṣṭhānāt sarvatraivam bhaviṣyati || 7 ||",
              "translated_text": "Thus, by establishment in one's self, it will be everywhere",
              "segment_number": 81
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "glānir vilu.ṅthikā dehe tasyāścājñānataḥ sṛtiḥ |",
              "translated_text": "Weakness is a thief in the body, and its wandering is due to ignorance",
              "segment_number": 82
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tad unmeṣaviluptaṃ cet kutaḥ sā syād ahetukā || 8 ||",
              "translated_text": "If that is vanished in awakening, how can it be causeless?",
              "segment_number": 83
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ekacintāprasaktasya yataḥ syād aparodayaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "For one engrossed in single thought, how can there be another arising?",
              "segment_number": 84
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "unmeṣaḥ sa tu vijñeyaḥ svayaṃ tam upalakṣayet || 9 ||",
              "translated_text": "That awakening should be known, one should observe it oneself",
              "segment_number": 85
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ato bindur ato nādo rūpam asmād ato rasaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "From this, the point, from this the sound, from this the form, from this the essence",
              "segment_number": 86
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "pravartante 'cireṇaiva kṣobhakatvena dehinaḥ || 10 ||",
              "translated_text": "They proceed quickly, agitating the embodied",
              "segment_number": 87
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "didṛkṣayeva sarvārthān yadā vyāpyāvatiṣṭhate |",
              "translated_text": "When, as if desiring to see all things, it pervades and abides",
              "segment_number": 88
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tadā kiṃ bahunoktena svayam eva avabhotsyate || 11 ||",
              "translated_text": "Then, what is the use of speaking much? One will know it oneself",
              "segment_number": 89
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "prabuddhaḥ sarvadā tiṣṭhej jñānenālokya gocaram |",
              "translated_text": "Awakened, one should always remain, seeing the field with knowledge",
              "segment_number": 90
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "ekatrāropayet sarvaṃ tato 'nyena na pīḍyate || 12 ||",
              "translated_text": "Should place all in one, then not be afflicted by another",
              "segment_number": 91
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "śabdarāśisamutthasya śaktivargasya bhogyatām |",
              "translated_text": "The enjoyment of the group of powers arising from the mass of sounds",
              "segment_number": 92
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "kalāviluptavibhavo gataḥ san sa paśuḥ smṛtaḥ || 13 ||",
              "translated_text": "Having lost the wealth of art, gone, he is considered a bound soul",
              "segment_number": 93
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "parāmṛtarasāpāyas tasya yaḥ pratyayodbhavaḥ |",
              "translated_text": "The loss of supreme nectar, for him whose consciousness arises",
              "segment_number": 94
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tenāsvatantratām eti sa ca tanmātragocaraḥ || 14 ||",
              "translated_text": "By that, he attains non-independence, and he is in the domain of the elements",
              "segment_number": 95
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "svarūpāvaraṇe cāsya śaktayaḥ satatotthitāḥ |",
              "translated_text": "In the covering of his own form, the powers are always arising",
              "segment_number": 96
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yataḥ śabdānuvedhena na vinā pratyayodbhavaḥ || 15 ||",
              "translated_text": "Because without the penetration of sound, consciousness does not arise",
              "segment_number": 97
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "seyaṃ kriyātmikā śaktiḥ śivasya paśuvartinī |",
              "translated_text": "This is the action-based power, of <s>Śiva</s>, acting on the bound souls",
              "segment_number": 98
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bandhayitrī svamārgasthā jñāta siddhyupapādikā || 16 ||",
              "translated_text": "Binding, established in its own path, known to bring about success",
              "segment_number": 99
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "tanmātrodayarūpena mano 'haṃbuddhivartinā |",
              "translated_text": "In the form of the rise of the elements, existing in the mind, ego, and intellect",
              "segment_number": 100
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "puryaṣṭakena saṃruddhas taduttham pratyayodbhavam || 17 ||",
              "translated_text": "Restrained by the eight-fold city, the arising of consciousness from that",
              "segment_number": 101
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "bhuṅkte paravaśo bhogaṃ tadbhāvāt saṃsared ataḥ |",
              "translated_text": "Enjoys the experience, being dependent, from that state, he transmigrates",
              "segment_number": 102
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "saṃsṛtipralayasyāsya kāraṇaṃ sampracakṣmahe || 18 ||",
              "translated_text": "We explain the cause of this cycle of birth and dissolution",
              "segment_number": 103
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "yadā tv ekatra saṃrūḍhas tadā tasya layodayau |",
              "translated_text": "When indeed established in one, then his dissolution and arising",
              "segment_number": 104
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "niyacchan bhoktṛtām eti tataś cakreśvaro bhavet || 19 ||",
              "translated_text": "Restraining, he attains the state of enjoyer, then becomes the lord of the circle",
              "segment_number": 105
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "p",
          "attributes": {},
          "text": "caturtho niḥṣyandaḥ",
          "translated_text": "The fourth effusion",
          "segment_number": 106
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "agādhasaṃśayāmbhodhisamuttaraṇatārinīm |",
              "translated_text": "The one who ferries across the ocean of deep doubt",
              "segment_number": 107
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "vande vicitrārthapadāṃ citrāṃ tāṃ gurubhāratīm || 1 ||",
              "translated_text": "I bow to that varied, wondrous teacher, with diverse meanings",
              "segment_number": 108
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tag": "lg",
          "attributes": {},
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "labdhvāpy alabhyam etaj jñānadhanaṃ hṛdguhāntakṛtanihiteḥ |",
              "translated_text": "Having obtained even the unobtainable, this wealth of knowledge, hidden in the heart's cave",
              "segment_number": 109
            },
            {
              "tag": "l",
              "attributes": {},
              "text": "vasuguptavac chivāya hi bhavati sadā sarvalokasya || 2 ||",
              "translated_text": "Like <s>Vasugupta</s>, it indeed becomes for the good of all the world",
              "segment_number": 110
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tag": "div",
